From 83e508c722f17b79f0fd736c232b9beacdaf0913 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:08:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (backport for EOL
 7.4.33)

Upstream php-src commit 712e60f9ed "Avoid state corruption via bailout"
(Arnaud Le Blanc, Ilija Tovilo) from branch PHP-7.4-CVE-2026-109618-109619,
GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w / GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp.

Applied as is, minus the hunks this tree already carries: the
max_multipart_body_parts INI entry (main/main.c) and the three
body-parts hunks in main/rfc1867.c, which are identical here already.
NEWS/version bump left out.

Behaviour change: memory_limit exhaustion and allocation overflows no
longer raise a catchable fatal error; the process prints the fatal error
to stderr and _exit(1)s (php-fpm logs the child exit and respawns it).
Session upload progress is disabled unconditionally.

Not compiled or tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
