From 7e70261081773aca20e4e180eb45e28a8d2b1011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:20:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Build against OpenSSL 4.x (keeps 1.1-3.x working)

OpenSSL 4.0 (and 4.1, API-compatible) removed APIs that ext/openssl
still used, so the build failed against dev-libs/openssl-4.1.0:

- ASN1_STRING is opaque and ASN1_STRING_data() is gone: use
  ASN1_STRING_get0_data()/ASN1_STRING_length() (old macro for < 1.1).
- OPENSSL_NO_SSL3 is no longer defined because SSLv3 was removed
  entirely; define it for >= 4.0 so SSLv3 stays "unavailable" as with
  1.1-3.x builds (otherwise the sslv3:// transport is registered).
- ERR_NUM_ERRORS is no longer exported; it only sizes PHP's own error
  ring buffer, keep the 1.0-3.x value 16.

Tested in a throwaway build container (gcc 16, Arch Linux): builds against OpenSSL 4.1.0 and
3.6.5; TLS smoke (tls/tlsv1.2 wrappers, pinned TLSv1_2 client and
server refusing 1.3, IP SAN peer_name, x509_parse) identical on both;
phpt ext/openssl+ftp+phar: patched vs 4.1 and patched vs 3.6 fail no
test that orig vs 3.6 passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
