From 3049c984ddb90ceca5a2ce68207e9b610f8d9ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:49:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv (CVE-2026-129496): DATEG(tzcache)
 use-after-free

In non-ZTS builds an error written to a file error_log during module
startup formatted its timestamp in the local timezone, which allocated
DATEG(tzcache) in startup memory that is freed at the end of startup.
An early request-startup diagnostic (e.g. max_input_vars exceeded) then
used the stale cache before date RINIT reset it. Format error log
timestamps in UTC unless modules are activated and the executor is
active.

Backport of php-src cb20015e04 for EOL 7.4.33. The main/main.c change
is identical (only the surrounding context differs: php_flock(fd, 2)).
The zend_test.warn_on_startup INI added upstream is not backported; the
7.4 test triggers the startup diagnostic with an invalid
session.sid_length instead (a session configuration warning is one of
the triggers named in the advisory) and matches 7.4's
"Warning: Unknown: Input variables exceeded" message.
Side effect (same as upstream): lines logged outside an active request
(startup/shutdown) now carry a UTC timestamp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
