From 47f12c2ca535de1ed811e80b3cb0f4f0806bcd0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:52:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg (CVE-2026-15353): out-of-bounds read
 on empty SOAP-ENC:arraySize

calc_dimension_12() returned 0 for an arraySize without any number
(empty, blank, "abc"), and the callers then walked a zero-sized position
array. Treat it as one dimension.

Backport of php-src 382d249480 for EOL 7.4.33. The C change is
identical (applies with offset). Tests: GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg.phpt uses
strpos() instead of str_contains(); GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg-wsdl.phpt drops
constructor property promotion and the ?string return type on
__doRequest() (PHP 8 only). The .wsdl fixture is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
