 	ps_globals->serializer = NULL;
 	ps_globals->mod_data = NULL;
+	ps_globals->rfc1867_enabled = 0;
 	ps_globals->session_status = php_session_none;
 	ps_globals->default_mod = NULL;
 	ps_globals->mod_user_implemented = 0;
From e5b64eb0beee5ca35f5f160c49dbd1f3236bc635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:28:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-3qrf-m4j2-pcrr (CVE-2023-3823): reset libxml2 global
 defaults before parsing

libxml2 copies process-wide defaults (xmlSubstituteEntitiesDefault,
xmlLoadExtDtdDefaultValue, validation, ...) into every new parser context.
If anything in the process changed one of them, for example another
extension or library, PHP's XML parsers (dom, simplexml, xmlreader, xsl,
soap, xml) inherited it even though PHP never asked for it. Entity
substitution and external DTD loading turned on that way allow XXE.

The fix sets the defaults to known values around each parse
(PHP_LIBXML_SANITIZE_GLOBALS / PHP_LIBXML_RESTORE_GLOBALS) or sets the
options on the parser context directly.

Backport of php-src c283c3ab0b (Niels Dossche) with the zend_test helper
backport (zend_test_override_libxml_global_state, Remi Collet) that the
upstream tests use; zend_test is a test-only extension. Same change as
Sury's 7.4 patches 0068 and 0070.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
