From 6107477a3fd41d8b5dd7c850e82c8c6987625055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:26:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CVE-2023-0568: one-byte overrun when appending a slash to
 paths

open_basedir checking (main/fopen_wrappers.c), DOMDocument and
XMLReader append a slash to a resolved path that can already be
MAXPATHLEN long, writing one byte past the stack buffer. The buffers
grow by one byte; the path length limit is unchanged, so no new
open_basedir failures.

Backport of php-src ec10b28d64 (Niels Dossche). Same change as Sury's
7.4 patch 0058.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
