From eb42686eaa4f51454e7e53fcb80690bd99ff3f92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:26:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-xr7j-rvgx-xq5p (CVE-2026-91767): wildcard name OOB
 read

The memchr() length underflowed when the wildcard prefix and suffix
overlapped in the subject name (CN "a*aaaa" against peer "aaaa"), so a
TLS peer could make the client read past the buffer.

Backport of php-src 78cc82b37a (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.4 patch 0146.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
